# cmd.exe's batch parser expects CRLF line endings. Whether a checkout gets
# them otherwise depends on the per-clone `core.autocrlf` setting: a clone made
# with `autocrlf=input` (or false) writes these files out LF-only, and cmd.exe
# then loses its line offsets and starts executing fragments of lines - the bug
# fixed alongside this file. `text eol=crlf` normalises to LF in the repository
# and always writes CRLF on checkout, whatever the clone's settings are.
#
# Keep the .bat files ASCII-only as well: cmd.exe decodes a batch file with the
# active console codepage (936 on a Chinese Windows), so a UTF-8 comment can
# consume a CR byte even with the endings right. See the header of build.bat.
*.bat text eol=crlf